# Round 104: BOXED_RET_BUILTINS was a 24-name hand-maintained allowlist
# against a runtime registering ~238 builtins, and it decided a
# function's DECLARED RETURN TYPE. A builtin not on the list was taken
# as "not boxed", so `return json_path of [j, k]` declared the function
# double and the string died through aot_num_ck_at at RUNTIME: rc 0 ->
# rc 1, nothing printed. No AOT: refusal, so the round-103 stdlib BUILD
# sweep could not see it -- lib/json.eigs is one of the 65 modules that
# BUILD, and it printed nothing and died on the first call through its
# own documented API.
#
# The polarity was backwards. An allowlist of the BOXED ones makes every
# builtin nobody thought of -- and every builtin upstream adds later --
# a silent latent instance. The return class now defaults to BOXED,
# which is always correct because a number boxes fine, and the NUMERIC
# ones are the enumerated exception: an omission costs a make_num
# instead of a miscompile. Every name in NUM_RET_BUILTINS was MEASURED
# against the pin with `type of`, not assumed.
#
# THE SWEEP CAUGHT THIS FIX'S OWN REGRESSION, one round after being
# committed: inverting the polarity made lib/checksum.eigs and
# lib/datetime.eigs stop building, because `buf_get` and `num` are
# genuinely numeric and were missing from the measured list, so their
# functions declared Value* while the call sites still emitted double.
# Note the direction -- a missing NUM_RET entry is a LOUD gcc error the
# gate catches, where a missing BOXED entry was a silent runtime death.
# That asymmetry is the whole point of the inversion.
#
# Why fixtures could not see it either: what rescues the shape is an
# unrelated boxed return ELSEWHERE in the same function, so any function
# with a string literal on some other return path masks it. Per
# invariant 22 the cases below vary the RETURN CLASS of the builtin --
# str, list, num -- and include the masked shape as the control.
doc is "{\"a\": \"hi\"}"
define get_str(j, k) as:
    return json_path of [j, k]
print of (get_str of [doc, "a"])
define get_type(v) as:
    return type of v
print of (get_type of 5)
xs is [1, 2, 3, 4]
define get_list(a) as:
    return list_slice of [a, 1, 3]
print of (get_list of xs)
b is zeros of 4
define get_shape(a) as:
    return shape of a
print of (get_shape of b)
define get_num(x) as:
    return sqrt of x
print of (get_num of 16)
define get_len(a) as:
    return len of a
print of (get_len of xs)
define masked(v, flag) as:
    if flag == 1:
        return "N"
    return type of v
print of (masked of [5, 0])
print of (masked of [5, 1])
